five o'clock, she received another anonymous note: If you are wise, you'll see that it's madness

34
00:04:09.574 --> 00:04:15.118
to sing tonight. Tell the managers you have a bad cold. Carlotta shrugged and sang a

35
00:04:15.119 --> 00:04:21.023
few notes to reassure herself that all was well. That night Carlotta went to the opera

36
00:04:21.024 --> 00:04:27.292
house, ready to sing the role of Marguerite. Moncharmin and Richard took their seats in box

37
00:04:27.293 --> 00:04:35.953
five, ready to meet the ghost. Soon after the performance began, Richard leaned over and joked,

38
00:04:35.954 --> 00:04:44.044
"So, has the ghost whispered anything in your ear?" Moncharmin chuckled. "Not yet, but you know

39
00:04:44.045 --> 00:04:53.045
he never appears until the middle of the first act." The first act passed without incident,

40
00:04:53.046 --> 00:04:58.014
but then, as any opera fan knows, Marguerite does not sing in that act. "Well, that's

41
00:04:58.015 --> 00:05:02.586
one act finished!" Moncharmin said. "Yes, and the ghost is late," Richard said. Moncharmin smiled. "We

42
